<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Fleeing</h1>
<p>SKILL
</p><p>Taught from the start of the guild by:
</p>
<pre> Thieves, Rangers, Assassins (up to 100%)
 Druids (80%)
 Fighters, Barbarians (70%)
 Conjurers, Healers, Necromancers, Sorcerers (60%)
</pre>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>flee</a>   (while fighting)
</pre>
<p>If you're really in bad shape, if you really want to get out of a fight NOW, use 
the flee command. Beware, you flee in a direction you can't choose:
you might end up somewhere worse!
</p><p>Fleeing takes endurance, and you can't flee when you are too exhausted. The 
better your flee skill, dexterity and wits against your enemy's, the better your 
chance. A bad try can leave you in a panic and still in the fight, or let your 
enemy strike you as you run.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Wimpy Mode</a>
</pre>




</div>